<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Senate of Milan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1499">1499</a>–<a href="/years/1786">1786</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Senate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> was the supreme court and highest council of the Duchy of Milan, created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a> in 1499 after his conquest of the duchy. It survived under the last Sforza dukes and under Spanish rule, registering and interpreting laws and guarding local legal traditions. Joseph II abolished it in 1786 as part of his reforms of Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/senate-of-milan.jpg" alt="Senate of Milan" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Gonin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:I_promessi_sposi_792.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
